# Crosswalk Mappings and Provenance Chains
# @xwalk resolves legacy, external, and customer terms to canonical IDs.
# Edge properties carry full epistemic provenance on every fact.

# --- Vocabulary (required when using predicates in @rel / @edges) ---

@vocab
  depends_on     | skill cannot be effectively applied without target present
  adjacent_to    | skills frequently co-occur and complement; symmetric
  progression_to | target represents natural advancement from source; not symmetric
  conflicts_with | skills rarely co-occur; inverse signal for co-occurrence modeling
  supersedes     | source makes target largely redundant; lifecycle transition signal
  composed_of    | source capability is constituted by target skills as a set


# --- Crosswalk identity resolution ---

@xwalk
  legacy:4421          => skill:workforce-planning [method:exact, type:asserted]
  onet:2.4.1           => skill:workforce-planning [method:mapped, conf:0.85, src:onet, type:asserted]
  customer:hr-planning => skill:workforce-planning [method:alias, type:asserted]
  customer:people-ops-plan => skill:workforce-planning
    [method:resolved, conf:0.9, type:inferred, rule:customer-resolution-v2]


# --- Instance edges with full provenance ---

@edges skill:workforce-planning

  # Asserted edge — explicitly validated by SME panel, confirmed against O*NET
  skill:workforce-planning depends_on skill:data-analysis
    [str:0.8, conf:high, status:validated, type:asserted,
     provenance:inferred:relationship-miner-v2 -> reviewed:sme-panel-2026Q1 -> validated:onet]

  # Inferred edge — derived by rule, proposed status pending review
  skill:workforce-planning adjacent_to skill:org-design
    [str:0.6, conf:medium, status:proposed, type:inferred, rule:adjacency-miner-v2]

  # Context-scoped edge — only valid in healthcare industry context
  skill:workforce-planning depends_on skill:regulatory-knowledge
    [str:0.7, conf:high, when:industry=healthcare, type:asserted, src:sme]
